648
00:37:40.278 --> 00:37:49.217
What L1 shows: equal share algorithms give a degraded backend more than it can serve, so its queue and your tail latency grow without bound.

649
00:37:49.497 --> 00:37:54.638
Load-aware algorithms (least-outstanding, P2C) cut its share automatically.

650
00:37:54.918 --> 00:37:59.078
