737
00:44:59.791 --> 00:45:06.959
SLOW-ALL-CLIENTS-IN-ZONE-A: even if every caller is in zone a, load-aware spill-over keeps latency healthy.

738
00:45:08.309 --> 00:45:09.013
Bug:

739
00:45:09.293 --> 00:45:11.170
What the first simulation run caught.

740
00:45:11.450 --> 00:45:19.045
The first version preferred the local zone whenever ≥ 70 % of its pods were healthy, ignoring load.

741
00:45:19.325 --> 00:45:29.095
With all callers in one zone, 100 % of traffic went to 4 of 10 pods, and latency exploded (p50 150 s in the simulation).

742
00:45:29.375 --> 00:45:41.066
Zone preference must include a load check (localZoneMaxLoadRatio), or zone affinity turns into a self-inflicted outage whenever callers aren't spread evenly across zones.

