760
00:47:01.062 --> 00:47:04.795
It runs to 26 lines; the full listing is in the chapter.

761
00:47:05.075 --> 00:47:10.771
1) Internal testers (header set by the BFF for staff accounts) always hit the canary.

762
00:47:11.051 --> 00:47:12.310
2) Everyone else:

763
00:47:12.590 --> 00:47:16.089
95 or 5 split within the orders-read weight group.

764
00:47:16.369 --> 00:47:25.841
Promote by shifting weights (5, then 25, then 50, then 100) while comparing canary versus stable SLOs (Ch 26).

765
00:47:28.691 --> 00:47:29.437
Warning:

766
00:47:29.717 --> 00:47:32.213
Weight routing is per request, not per user.

767
00:47:32.493 --> 00:47:35.992
A user can bounce between versions on successive requests.

768
00:47:36.272 --> 00:47:47.813
If the versions differ visibly (new UI data, new fields), route canaries by user hash (a custom predicate on X-User-Id) so each user sees one version consistently.

769
00:47:48.093 --> 00:47:55.965
And strip X-Canary from external clients (add it to IdentityHeadersFilter.STRIP) so outsiders can't opt into the canary.

770
00:47:57.315 --> 00:47:58.126
