773
00:48:06.741 --> 00:48:07.488
Note:

774
00:48:07.768 --> 00:48:10.413
ADR-032 or 033:

775
00:48:10.693 --> 00:48:16.133
Latency-aware P2C with ejection; gateway-only, idempotent-only retries.

776
00:48:16.413 --> 00:48:17.331
Context.

777
00:48:17.611 --> 00:48:26.229
Round-robin kept sending traffic to a slow-but-healthy pod, failing ~40 % of multi-call checkouts (§1.1).

778
00:48:26.509 --> 00:48:29.133
Retries were unbounded and included POSTs.

779
00:48:30.483 --> 00:48:31.358
Decision.

780
00:48:31.638 --> 00:48:38.657
(1) The gateway and service clients use P2C scored by (in-flight + 1) times peak-EWMA latency.

781
00:48:38.937 --> 00:48:48.046
(2) Passive outlier ejection after 5 consecutive failures, for 30 s doubling to 5 min, with at most 50 % of a pool ejected.

782
00:48:48.326 --> 00:48:59.782
(3) Zone preference with a health check (≥ 70 % of local pods healthy) and a load check (local average in-flight at most 1.25 times fleet).

783
00:49:00.062 --> 00:49:05.331
(4) Readiness reflects instance-local health, and liveness never checks dependencies.

784
00:49:05.611 --> 00:49:08.427
(5) The gateway is the only retrying layer:

785
00:49:08.707 --> 00:49:14.958
GET or idempotent only, one retry on a different instance, jittered, within a 10 % budget.

786
00:49:15.238 --> 00:49:17.691
Clients retry writes with Idempotency-Key.

787
00:49:17.971 --> 00:49:22.750
(6) Canaries by weight groups, and by user hash when versions differ visibly.

788
00:49:24.100 --> 00:49:25.124
Consequences.

789
00:49:25.404 --> 00:49:29.969
(+) Degraded pods lose traffic within seconds without operator action.

790
00:49:30.249 --> 00:49:34.281
(+) There are no duplicate side effects from infrastructure retries.

791
00:49:34.561 --> 00:49:39.831
(minus ) We own balancer code (mitigated by the simulation harness and unit tests).

792
00:49:40.111 --> 00:49:47.812
(minus ) The per-instance state resets on gateway pod restarts, which is acceptable because EWMA converges within seconds.

793
00:49:48.092 --> 00:50:00.508
Revisit when: the service mesh (Ch 17) provides equivalent balancing (Envoy: least-request with P2C, outlier detection, zone-aware routing) for service-to-service traffic.

794
00:50:00.788 --> 00:50:04.628
The gateway keeps this adapter only if mesh ingress isn't adopted.

